<description>&lt;p&gt;The Burkina Faso junta has restored the death penalty for terrorism and treason while securing pilot training from a Czech state firm, and its army and Russia's Africa Corps face fresh accusations of civilian killings. In northern Niger gunmen attacked buses, killing at least 12 people, and two European women were freed after kidnapping, while a US missionary held for nine months was released. Mali’s army and Russian fighters are also accused of new civilian abuses. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiY0FVX3lxTFA4eFFtbFV4MUhtcS1TWld0bGdkWFlKY2pZU3U2cUgyTENPNFg2QnFHVUE1YW5FQi1WWW02RUY5WmNBejF0ZXl4dXJMaWw5aU9ZUzBEcHJHTTZ3VVdjcXpqSjYzZ9IBY0FVX3lxTFA4eFFtbFV4MUhtcS1TWld0bGdkWFlKY2pZU3U2cUgyTENPNFg2QnFHVUE1YW5FQi1WWW02RUY5WmNBejF0ZXl4dXJMaWw5aU9ZUzBEcHJHTTZ3VVdjcXpqSjYzZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxOOUVqNllZMWlndnZmX3dxamhYM25iZ3FIemFyRy1sbFB0cHhkY2RfQkpkaldkWHA0ZVFEclJpRnZGeXVlNXp5Tnh5RjRiTGRQeGN1eUlhNXM5RWNCRmpwRWRUQldHX25PWjVES2xmREpaaW5vQUZlZmFybldfV1JNQU1OdUpzOFVHN1NhX2xDeDNxOEpBSGUyel9MbDBNUkpKc3l3TnNqNkh3NjVZLTh4UnlvTVFycjNp?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxPRDhKTTlnTVFYd3l3M3VlTHNiMXNwNE9GdkRBeGg1ZXk2eUVnRUl2c3V3Z1ZrZTk2djJLeGhIb3A1NlpTeWs2UWFtYkdhLXJjUS1aTVBfcHE2eGFwR21YdDhBOTlUVXpyb3pnX0xGRkpXaDNCM2c2LTJsNDVlaXFDUy14SWItaW5jOVBabDZZMF82em5oN2hHaFU4Vm90Tm5oVGV4ZVUzUkxLc0l0b2xTVUphUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxQYmUzOGh6M3NORy05MGZVZlV0YzFTVnN6Wk1lM1dUTm00dmowdVBDaEExakFZS1loTDNHZ0c5SW50dWFtbzVpTGloOGFLMGhOVElwMWVVN25CZTFYcUVfOXppdktKRGozOE42TWpPcHRySjNlS3RlSHhsTFdvRmZVej